  "description": "protoc tooling that generates synchronous TCP packet-handler service bases\n      (IPacketHandler / [PacketHandler(MsgId)] / Connection) instead of gRPC HTTP/2 stubs,\n      via a forked grpc_csharp_plugin. Depends on Grpc.Tools for protoc and the message codegen.\n      Windows-x64 only in this version.",
  "developmentDependency": true,
  "id": "Raphael.Tcp.Tools",
  "isPrerelease": false,
  "lastEdited": "2026-05-31T06:20:35.257Z",
  "licenseExpression": "Apache-2.0",
  "licenseUrl": "https://licenses.nuget.org/Apache-2.0",
  "listed": true,
  "packageHash": "QLMGlakwpyhTLR24auw08ccVRKIC7Y31snFuUKtf/1Yi8ulW3JDaliH62bYNplpFFzTZhZ6lT/XWJ+ApTBMo1Q==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 1426668,
  "published": "2026-05-31T06:18:27.197Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.2.0: breaking TCP codegen shape changes - remove wrapper service class, rename generated base class to <ServiceNameWithoutService>HandlerBase, derive MsgId from request/response message names with CS_/SC_ normalization and configurable msgid_prefix (TcpMsgIdPrefix). 1.1.2: fix TCP protoc invocation to include protobuf well-known imports path (google/protobuf/* now resolves, including Empty->void scenarios). 1.1.1: add changelog/release notes. 1.1.0: google.protobuf.Empty response now maps to a C# void handler (no auto-reply); dropped the Raphael prefix from all build properties (RaphaelTcp* -> Tcp*) - breaking for consuming csproj. See CHANGELOG.md.",
